## Packages

x86-64 and arm64 packages for PostgreSQL 17, 18 and 19 are attached below (`SHA256SUMS` covers every asset); other versions build from source with `make USE_PGXS=1`.

- Debian 12 and 13, Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 (PGDG `postgresql-N`, N = 17, 18 or 19): `sudo apt install ./postgresql-N-pg-sift_@VERSION@-1_amd64.deb` (`_arm64.deb` on arm64)
- RHEL, Rocky, Alma 9 and 10 (PGDG `postgresqlN-server`): `sudo dnf install ./pg_sift_N-@VERSION@-1.el9.x86_64.rpm` (`.aarch64.rpm` on arm64)
- Amazon Linux 2023 (the distribution's `postgresqlN-server`, N = 17 or 18): `sudo dnf install ./pg_sift_N-@VERSION@-1.amzn2023.x86_64.rpm` (`.aarch64.rpm` on arm64)
- Arch Linux: AUR `pg_sift`.

Every change: [CHANGELOG.md](https://github.com/brauliobo/pg_sift/blob/v@VERSION@/CHANGELOG.md).

## SQLite extension

pg_sift for SQLite @VERSION@ (`sift`, a loadable extension; a separate component from the PostgreSQL extension above). Rebuilt with the PostgreSQL @VERSION@ release: no change to the SQL interface or the shared format.

- **No change:** the changes of this release are in the PostgreSQL column index, which is not in this extension. No speed-up or slow-down is claimed.
- Needs SQLite 3.38 or newer; Linux x86-64, glibc 2.34 or newer. Built on Debian 12, loaded into the SQLite of Debian 12, Ubuntu 24.04 and AlmaLinux 10 before release.
- Storage format 2: tables of 3.4.0 to 3.7.0 open as they are, nothing to rebuild.

Download `sift-sqlite-@VERSION@-linux-x86_64.tar.gz` (below, covered by `SHA256SUMS` with the packages), unpack it and `.load ./sift` from the `sqlite3`
shell (`sha256sum --ignore-missing -c SHA256SUMS`). Documentation: [sqlite/README.md](https://github.com/brauliobo/pg_sift/blob/v@VERSION@/sqlite/README.md).
Every change: [sqlite/CHANGELOG.md](https://github.com/brauliobo/pg_sift/blob/v@VERSION@/sqlite/CHANGELOG.md).

## MariaDB extension

pg_sift for MariaDB @VERSION@ (`sift`, a UDF library and two SQL files; a separate component from the extensions above). Rebuilt with the PostgreSQL @VERSION@ release: no change to the SQL files.

- **No change:** the changes of this release are in the PostgreSQL column index, which is not in this extension. No speed-up or slow-down is claimed.
- One library per MariaDB series, because it calls the server's own symbols and refuses to load into another series: 10.11, 11.4, 11.8, 12.1 and 13.0; Linux x86-64. Each was built in the stock `mariadb:<series>` image against that server's headers and loaded into a server of the same image before release. `BUILD-INFO` in the tarball lists the server version and the glibc each library needs.
- Index format 2: an index of 3.4.0 to 3.7.0 opens as it is, nothing to rebuild.

Download `sift-mariadb-@VERSION@-linux-x86_64.tar.gz` (below, covered by `SHA256SUMS` with the packages), unpack it, copy `lib/<series>/libsift_udf.so` of your server's series
(`SELECT VERSION()`) into its `plugin_dir`, then `SOURCE sql/functions.sql` once per server and `sql/sift.sql` once per database (`sha256sum --ignore-missing -c SHA256SUMS`).
Documentation: [mariadb/README.md](https://github.com/brauliobo/pg_sift/blob/v@VERSION@/mariadb/README.md).
Every change: [mariadb/CHANGELOG.md](https://github.com/brauliobo/pg_sift/blob/v@VERSION@/mariadb/CHANGELOG.md).


